title: S2D/HCI monitoring
agents: windows
catalog: storage/hci
license: PolyForm Internal Use 1.0.0
distribution: check_mk

description:
 This package monitors Windows Failover Cluster, Microsoft virtualization workloads,
 Storage Spaces Direct, and HCI components using split Checkmk Windows agent plug-ins.
 It is compatible with Checkmk 2.5.0 and newer and uses Check API V2.

item:
 Services are itemized by node name, network name, CSV name, storage pool name,
 virtual disk name, physical disk serial number, storage job name, workload name,
 workload integration service, workload network adapter, workload disk, and retained
 recovery point/checkpoint name depending on the section.

inventory:
 Services are discovered from the following sections when valid JSON lines are
 present:

 <<<s2d_hci_nodes>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_networks>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_quorum>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_csv>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_storage_pools>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_virtual_disks>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_physical_disks>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_storage_jobs>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_virtualization_host>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_virtualization_workloads>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_virtualization_services>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_virtualization_replication>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_virtualization_checkpoints>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_virtualization_network_adapters>>>
 <<<s2d_hci_virtualization_hard_disks>>>

examples:
 Example section line:

 <<<s2d_hci_nodes>>>
 {"name":"NODE01","state":"Up","node_weight":1,"dynamic_weight":1,"drain_status":"NotInitiated"}

 <<<s2d_hci_virtualization_workloads>>>
 {"name":"VM01","state":"Running","cpu_usage":12,"memory_assigned":8589934592,"memory_demand":6442450944}

perfdata:
 The package emits metrics for CSV free percentage, volume free percentage, pool
 allocated bytes, storage job percentage, workload CPU usage, workload memory
 pressure, and retained recovery point/checkpoint age. Each emitted metric has a
 Graphing API V1 definition.

parameters:
 The ruleset s2d_hci_csv configures CSV free-space lower warning and critical
 thresholds. The default levels are 15 percent warning and 10 percent critical.
 The ruleset s2d_hci_volumes configures volume free-space lower warning and
 critical thresholds. The workload ruleset configures CPU and memory pressure
 upper thresholds for workload services.

troubleshooting:
 Verify that the Windows agent output contains the expected sections. Verify that
 FailoverClusters, Storage, and Hyper-V modules are available on the monitored
 cluster node. Use Checkmk agent plug-in caching instead of adding sleeps to the
 PowerShell scripts.

 Tested Checkmk version range: 2.5.0 and newer.
 Recommended cache intervals:
 - s2d_hci_fast.ps1: 60-120 seconds
 - s2d_hci_storage.ps1: 300 seconds
 - s2d_hci_jobs.ps1: 300 seconds
 - s2d_hci_health.ps1: 600 seconds
 - s2d_hci_perf.ps1: 900 seconds
 - s2d_hci_virtualization.ps1: 120-300 seconds

 Installation: install and enable the s2d_hci_monitoring MKP, deploy the required
 Windows collectors, reload Checkmk, and rediscover services on a test host first.
 Removal: disable and remove the MKP, remove host-side collector and scheduled-task
 files, then reload the Checkmk site.
